{
  "mn85:0.1": "Middle Discourses 85 ",
  "mn85:0.2": "With Prince Bodhi ",
  "mn85:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn85:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying in the land of the Bhaggas at Crocodile’s Bellow, in the deer park at Bhesakaḷā’s Wood. ",
  "mn85:2.1": "Now at that time a new stilt longhouse named Pink Lotus had recently been constructed for Prince Bodhi. It had not yet been occupied by an ascetic or brahmin or any human at all. ",
  "mn85:3.1": "Then Prince Bodhi addressed the student Sañjikāputta, ",
  "mn85:3.2": "“Please, dear Sañjikāputta, go to the Buddha, and in my name bow with your head to his feet. Ask him if he is healthy and well, nimble, strong, and living comfortably. ",
  "mn85:3.3": "",
  "mn85:3.4": "And then ask him whether he ",
  "mn85:3.5": "would accept tomorrow’s meal from me together with the mendicant Saṅgha.” ",
  "mn85:4.1": "“Yes, worthy sir,” Sañjikāputta replied. He did as Prince Bodhi asked, and ",
  "mn85:4.2": "",
  "mn85:4.3": "",
  "mn85:4.4": "",
  "mn85:4.5": "",
  "mn85:4.6": "the Buddha consented with silence. ",
  "mn85:4.7": "Then, knowing that the Buddha had consented, Sañjikāputta rose from his seat, went to Prince Bodhi, and said, ",
  "mn85:4.8": "“I gave your message to the worthy Gotama, ",
  "mn85:4.9": "",
  "mn85:4.10": "",
  "mn85:4.11": "",
  "mn85:4.12": "and he accepted.” ",
  "mn85:5.1": "And when the night had passed Prince Bodhi had delicious fresh and cooked foods prepared in his own home. He also had the Pink